# sha256 of data/willeq.db, the shipped SQLite database. Rebuilt by
# scripts/build_willeq_db.sh from ten inputs: the EQ client's spells_us.txt,
# eqstr_us.txt, dbstr_us.txt, SoundAssets.txt, AnimationSounds.txt,
# mp3index.txt and eqlsstr_us.txt, plus data/item_models.json,
# data/equipment_models.json and config/race_models.json. 29,791 rows across
# eleven tables, metadata.version = 7 (kWilleqDbExpectedVersion).
#
# T454 (board B474) dropped the twelfth table, equipment_textures (2,623 rows
# nothing read -- the equipment texture path resolves live through
# EquipmentModelLoader::buildEquipmentIndex()), which is the whole of the
# difference from T450's 32,414. metadata.input_digest did NOT move: the
# inputs are the same bytes, only the loader changed.
#
# T450 (board B467) made the file reproducible in the first place: the builder
# used to stamp metadata.build_date = __DATE__ " " __TIME__, so recompiling it
# changed these bytes with identical inputs and no pin was possible. That row
# is now metadata.input_digest, a path-independent digest of the inputs.
#
# Pinned here so an input drift, or a hand-edit of the database, is a ctest
# FAIL (DbReproducible). Update this line in the SAME commit that changes an
# input -- exactly like data/willeq.eqe1.sha256 and data/textures.sha256.
d503b95227d4f827595e30ce7e6175ce65c8007d8d2ba3eadf7095d6734afa25  willeq.db
